# Round-30 Fix C — alias-chain shape (adv_aliaschain).
#
# A transitive chain of bare-assigns off a single heap-owned String:
# `String b = a; String c = b; String d = c`, all live to scope exit.
# Under the old Branch A each hop SharedHeap-tagged + unregistered its
# source's drop while the backend deep-copied — leaking the intermediate
# buffers. The Branch C CoW path aliases each hop to the ONE owned buffer
# (severed only on mutation), so there is exactly one allocation and one
# drop across the whole chain → ASan-clean.

void main():
    String x = "chain-"
    String y = "owned-tail"
    String owned = x + y       # single heap-owned buffer
    String b = owned           # hop 1 (was Branch A)
    String c = b               # hop 2
    String d = c               # hop 3
    print(owned)
    print(b)
    print(c)
    print(d)
